OL,3,GNEWSAExxonMobil fined #267,000 over
OL,4,Achemical leaks at Mossmorran
OL,5,
OL,6,FPetrochemicals giant ExxonMobil has
OL,7,Fbeen fined #267,000 over leaks of
OL,8,Fdangerous substances caused by corroded
OL,9,Fpiping at its plant in Fife.
OL,11,FThe Health and Safety Executive (HSE)
OL,12,Fsaid dimethyl sulphide and ethane was
OL,13,Freleased from overhead pipes at the
OL,14,FMossmorran facility near Cowdenbeath in
OL,15,F2018 and 2019.
OL,17,FAn investigation found the company had
OL,18,Fbeen aware of one pipe leaking the
OL,19,Fsubstances, which are irritable to the
OL,20,Feyes and harmful if ingested, for four
OL,21,Fmonths while workers were on site
OL,22,Fwithout taking action.
OL,23,APub: 26-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB  Scot NewsC Reg TVF  Weather
FL,425,420,260,160,0,100
